From 2ba37051ea0d938c3b8ed0dac4c2951a4960da8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:55:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: S-X8 integer-dot mat-vec against Q8_1 activations
 (R46 commit C)

Adds mul_mat_vec_sx8_q8_1_f32: one call consumes a whole 32-weight S-X8 block
against a whole Q8_1 activation block, so the header, the four range strategies
and the two planes are read once each.

The affine decode w = rlo_s + step_s * L is fixed per 8-weight sub-block, so a
sub-block needs TWO integer sums, sum(L*q) and sum(q). The Q8_1 ds.y term cannot
stand in for sum(q) because rlo changes every 8 weights. sum(q) is a dot against
0x01010101, the same instruction with no extra loads. Levels are in [0,63] and
quants in [-127,127], so 63*127*4 = 32004 per call cannot overflow the 32-bit
accumulator.

Decode constants stay in sx8_range() / sx8_levels4() (types.glsl), shared with
the float mat-vec and dequant_sx8 -- the F-110 single-home rule.

ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq() admits S-X8 at every width for now: the per-width
table this lane measures is what narrows it, and narrowing before the
measurement would hide the widths that lose. Any width that loses at op level
must be excluded there before this ships.

The mmq_int_dot ARIFI-SYNC-SET marker carries EXCEPT SX8: no id q8_1 pipeline
is generated for S-X8 (the mat-vec-id path is f32-B only, as its src0_types
switch already records), so admitting it in the _id mirror would select a null
pipeline.

Correctness on the built binary (arm c, foreground, quiet hold): MUL_MAT
type_a=sx8 12/12 OK, MUL_MAT_ID 2/2, GET_ROWS and CPY 2/2 backends passed,
test-quantize-fns unchanged at the 6 pre-existing non-sx8 failures. A planted
RED in this dot product turned n=1..8 red on every shape and left n=9 and n=64
green, which proves the new pipeline is the one executing at every mat-vec
width rather than a silent fallback.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
WI: WI-1729
Lane: lane-230
Conflict-resolved: S6 strict auto_merge - wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS6_581.py)
